WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.370
Jerusalem, after the exile.

2
00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:06.210
The Temple stands again, but
the walls are still broken.

3
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:11.890
A priest and scribe, Ezra, hears that men
have married women of the peoples around.

4
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.810
He tears his clothes.

5
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.430
The men agree to send
away their foreign wives,

6
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:18.720
and even the children born to them.

7
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:23.320
Yet a prophet has God say:
Blessed be Egypt my people.

8
00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:27.960
So when leaders disagree in
God's name, who speaks for God?

9
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:33.500
In this mission, you'll see why a tiny
community with no king guarded its identity.

10
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.190
Then you'll weigh up
exclusion and inclusion,

11
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.050
then and now.

12
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.870
Your mission: weigh up who
spoke for God after the exile,

13
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.080
and how to judge.
